== test: gh478-runaway-guard ==
== 1. fast command: rc and stdout pass through untouched (red control) ==
  PASS: run_with_timeout returns 0 on a fast command
  PASS: stdout passes through
  PASS: child's own exit code propagates (7)
== 2. hung child: capped at the group, rc 124, wall clock bounded ==
  PASS: hung child capped with rc 124
  PASS: wall clock bounded (1s for a 1s cap)
  PASS: timeout message names the cap override
== 3. TERM-resistant grandchild cannot outlive the group kill (gh369 shape) ==
  PASS: leader capped with rc 124
  PASS: TERM-resistant grandchild (18703) is dead — the group kill reached it
== 4. LEADER-LESS group: leader exits normally, TERM-resistant descendant remains ==
  PASS: green suite with a leader-less surviving group exits 1
  PASS: TERM-resistant descendant of the exited leader is dead — the EXIT reaper reached it
== 5. reaper kills a tracked survivor and announces it ==
  PASS: reap reports that it had to kill
  PASS: kill announced with the group id
  PASS: tracked survivor is dead after reap
== 6. clean-exit child: reap is a no-op, no failure signal ==
  PASS: cleanly-exited group sets no failure signal
  PASS: no reap noise for a clean child
  PASS: no tracked group survives its own completion (dead entries forgotten)
== 7. composed EXIT trap: status-preserving, owner cleanup always runs ==
  PASS: green-but-reaped exits 1 (reaped child is a failure, loudly)
  PASS: owner cleanup ran on the reaped-green path
  PASS: the suite's own failure status is preserved (3)
  PASS: owner cleanup ran on the failing path
== 8. init refuses to steal a suite-owned EXIT trap, installs when free ==
  PASS: init refuses when the suite owns the EXIT trap
  PASS: init installs the composed trap when no EXIT trap exists
== 9. env override: ATE_WATCHDOG_TIMEOUT carries the cap ==
  PASS: 1s override cap stops a hung child (env contract)
== 10. witnessed mutation: timeout disabled → the cap case goes red ==
  PASS: mutant (timeout disabled) went red or was emergency-capped — never silently green (rc=0)
  PASS: the red control leaked no child group (unique sleeper gone)
== 11. static assertion: the bash lib owns NO kill implementation ==
  PASS: bash lib only probes (kill -0); killing stays in proc_group.py --kill-pgid
== 11. sweep: token-aware match, dry run signals nothing ==
  PASS: ate_runaway_sweep.py exists and is executable
  PASS: dry run lists the real ATE shape (age 0)
  PASS: spaced python -c import shape (the incident shape) is listed
  PASS: near-match and bare-substring processes are never listed
  PASS: dry run left the candidate alive
== 12. non-python interpreter before -c is refused (shape B interpreter gate) ==
  PASS: shape B requires a python-ish interpreter before -c
== 13. sweep --kill: TERM stops a cooperative target (--limit-pids containment) ==
  PASS: cooperative candidate stopped by --kill
== 13. sweep --kill escalates to SIGKILL on a TERM-resistant target ==
  PASS: TERM-resistant candidate killed after the grace window
  PASS: escalation waited out the configured grace
  PASS: escalation logged
== 14. age gate: a young candidate above --max-age-minutes is not touched ==
  PASS: age gate holds (etime < 1m excluded)
  PASS: young candidate untouched
== 15. sweep never lists itself or its ancestors ==
  PASS: self/ancestor exclusion holds
== 16. witnessed matcher mutations → red (baseline: GH-478-negative-control.md) ==
  PASS: broadened matcher caught by the near-match control (red witnessed)
  PASS: narrowed matcher caught by the signature control (red witnessed)
== 18. pgid publication fails CLOSED, never open ==
  PASS: proc_group kills the just-started group when pgid publication fails (rc 125)
  PASS: run_with_timeout refuses (rc 2) when the pgid scratch file cannot be created
== 17. identity recheck: lstart is load-bearing, containment alone never suffices ==
  PASS: identity = uid+lstart exact; command containment alone never signals
